{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"],"title":"Inherits From","kind":"relationships","type":"inheritsFrom"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"MutableDirectedGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph.swift#L54"},"modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}],"title":"MutableDirectedGraph","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols015MutableDirectedA0P","role":"symbol"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols021BidirectionalDirectedA0P","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P8VerticesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype","text":"Vertices"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A wrapper that adds a rule, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", can own any mutable directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation as its base through this protocol and work on it without extra hashing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each vertex has a key: its index in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"Vertices.Index == Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). On a dense","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representation (","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedPseudograph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") the key is the vertex’s slot, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"also its ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". On ","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it is the vertex’s position, which never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changes while the vertex exists and may leave holes. The underscored members read and write the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph by key, so a wrapper hashes a vertex once and then works on keys.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In addition to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"’s laws:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_key(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices.firstIndex(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_vertex(atKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is its inverse.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For a vertex with key ","type":"text"},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"_successors(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"_predecessors(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"_outEdges(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"_inEdges(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"_outDegree(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_inDegree(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equal the unprefixed members for that vertex.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"_successorKeys(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are the far ends’ keys, in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same order. ","type":"text"},{"code":"_sourceKey(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_targetKey(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are the endpoints’ keys.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertVertex(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" appends a vertex, which must not already be one, and returns its key,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.endIndex"},{"type":"text","text":" before the call. Keys of other vertices do not change."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"text":" inserts the edge and returns its position. On a simple graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"text":"), an edge already present is not inserted again and its position is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returned. Inserting an edge changes no key.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeVertex(atKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" removes the vertex and every edge at it. If the representation fills"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hole by moving another vertex in (a swap-remove), it returns that vertex’s old key, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that vertex’s key becomes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":". Otherwise it returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and no other key changes."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_removeEdge(at:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" removes the edge at a live position and returns it, and traps on any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position. Removing an edge changes no key.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeVertex(atKey: _key(of: v)!)"},{"type":"text","text":", returning the removed instance."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_built(vertices:sourceKeys:targetKeys:reportingPositions:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"_insertVertex(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for each vertex in order, then ","type":"text"},{"code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for each pair","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in order. It gives the same graph and the same position for each pair.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A wrapper may keep one table entry per 1024 keys, from the smallest live key to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"vertices.endIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", plus O(1) per live vertex. That matches the representation’s own page"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"table. On a dense representation the keys are "},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". On "},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"span can exceed the vertex count, because removals leave holes and a decoded graph may start at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any position. Its decoder bounds the span at "},{"code":"16 × vertexCount + 64","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" pages. Keys before the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smallest live key cost nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successorKeys(ofKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" return the stored rows typed as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuccessorIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PredecessorIndices"},{"type":"text","text":", whose elements here are keys. On a dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation keys and indices coincide. On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" the elements are positions,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which are vertex indices only while the graph has no holes. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successorIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then unavailable, but the key rows are not."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"insert(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is not a requirement because its return type varies by representation.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"(inserted:memberAfterInsert:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the multigraphs return the new","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position, and a wrapper that rejects edges returns an optional. Generic code inserts an edge by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key with ","type":"text"},{"code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The underscored members are for wrappers inside the library. Callers use the representations’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove"},{"type":"text","text":" members, which take vertices."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/insert(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(edge:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/init()":{"required":true,"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The empty graph."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()","role":"symbol","title":"init()","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/init()"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Vertex":{"fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","required":true,"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/vertex","role":"symbol","title":"Vertex"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Vertices-swift.associatedtype":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Vertices"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","text":"Collection"}],"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype","required":true,"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Vertices","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/vertices-swift.associatedtype","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"removeAll","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"keepingCapacity","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Removes every vertex and edge."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","required":true,"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/removeall(keepingcapacity:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/remove(edge:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"remove","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"edge","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedEdge","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedEdgeV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedEdge","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedEdgeV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Removes one copy of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edge"},{"type":"text","text":". On a representation with parallel edges it removes the newest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copy. Never inserts or removes a vertex."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(edge:)","required":true,"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"remove(edge:)","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/remove(edge:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/remove(_:)":{"required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Removes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" and every edge at it."}],"title":"remove(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/remove(_:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"remove","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols","role":"collection"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"DirectedGraph","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)":{"required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Reserves space for at least ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" vertices and ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" edges.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/reservecapacity(vertexcount:edgecount:)","title":"reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reserveCapacity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"vertexCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"edgeCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph":{"abstract":[{"text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate.","type":"text"}],"title":"MutableDirectedGraph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Removes every edge, keeping every vertex and its key."}],"type":"topic","title":"removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","required":true,"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"removeAllEdges"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"keepingCapacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/removealledges(keepingcapacity:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/insert(_:)":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Inserts ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with no edges, if it is not already a vertex.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"insert"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> (inserted"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":", memberAfterInsert"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/insert(_:)","kind":"symbol","title":"insert(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/insert(_:)","required":true},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"abstract":[{"text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods. In-adjacency usually costs extra","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"storage, so representations that store only out-adjacency conform to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"text":" alone.","type":"text"}],"title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph"}}}